# Date format in UI

Mandatory. Present and future.

## Standard format (absolute)

For dates/times **shown** to the user (not form inputs):

`d MMM, y hh:mm a`

Example: `9 jun, 2026 11:00 p. m.`

```ts
this.datePipe.transform(value, 'd MMM, y hh:mm a')
// or in template:
{{ value | date:'d MMM, y hh:mm a' }}
```

Date only: `d MMM, y` → `9 jun, 2026`
Time only: `hh:mm a` → `11:00 p. m.`

## Forbidden in visible text

- `dd/MM/yyyy`, `dd/MM/yyyy HH:mm`
- `yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm` in UI (allowed in APIs/controls)
- Native `datetime-local` display as a reading format

## Form inputs

- Editable date: `app-floating-date-picker` (corporate calendar)
- Editable time: `ion-input type="time"`
- Do not invent a `datetime-local` when the sibling module already uses separate date + time

## Relative

If the module already uses “Hace X min/h”, keep it; when switching to absolute, use the format above.
